;; world/rooms/glasswood/x-5y3.room
(room
  region: glasswood
  at: (-5 3)
  title: "Fall's Head"
  intent: "where the stream froze as it went over the edge, and the note you are following comes up from below"
  bed: (wind 0.7 water 0.3 hum 0.2 drone 0.4)
  grid:
  ("          |          |   "
   "          |          |   "
   "          |          |   "
   "          |          |   "
   "          |          |   "
   "          |          |   "
   "####  %=================="
   "####  %   |          |   "
   "####  %   |          |   "
   "####  %   |          |   "
   "####  %   |          |   ")
  decor: auto)
;; The stream froze on the shelf (columns 0-3) and its fall is the glass
;; wall (column 3) going down through the Frozen Fall to the Old Birch.
;; Between the glass and the rough rock (column 6) is the chimney
;; (columns 4-5), two wide: a hop across its mouth, or the way down. East
;; the crowns run on to the Crown Gap over the Frozen Fall's floor. H3's
;; tone comes up from below.
